    {
        "content": "<p>jrandolf opened <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wasmtime/pull/14869\">PR #14869</a> from <code>jrandolf:c-api-null-name</code> to <code>bytecodealliance:main</code>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Several functions in the component C API passed a name pointer and length straight to <code>std::slice::from_raw_parts</code>. That's UB for a null pointer even when the length is zero, which is exactly what the C++ API passes for a default <code>std::string_view</code>, and debug builds abort with \"unsafe precondition(s) violated\". There were 10 of these: the component and instance type lookups, the five linker <code>add_*</code> functions, and the two <code>get_export_index</code> functions. They now use the existing <code>slice_from_raw_parts</code> helper, like the rest of the C API.</p>\n<p>The new tests only crash without the fix in a debug build, which is what CI uses.<br>\n</p>\n</blockquote>",
